WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.222
Does a ratio below one mean faster, slower, or nothing at all?

q0002
00:00:06.222 --> 00:00:15.240
This episode has one job: A ratio has no honest direction until numerator, denominator, favorable direction, workload, boundary, and uncertainty are visible.

q0003
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:24.258
We build on Preparation, kernel, wrapper, and end-to-end time; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:24.258 --> 00:00:33.276
A ratio compares a named numerator with a named denominator; below one favors the numerator only for a time or cost ratio.

q0005
00:00:33.276 --> 00:00:40.460
Watch for the label numerator; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:47.163
When we say denominator, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:47.163 --> 00:00:55.309
The term ratio receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:00:55.309 --> 00:01:01.050
We will keep parity visible whenever its definition controls the inference.

q0009
00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:07.753
A persistent confidence interval label marks exactly where that object enters the example.

q0010
00:01:07.753 --> 00:01:16.380
The next sequence uses Four-variable truth layout as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0011
00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.198
Our stable example is Four-variable truth layout.

q0012
00:01:20.198 --> 00:01:29.216
F(A,B,C,D)=(A AND B) XOR (C OR D), row variables A,B, column variables C,D, MSB-first ordering.

q0013
00:01:29.216 --> 00:01:36.400
Carry assignments, live support, explicit CM, packed truth vectors, and exact output across episodes.

q0014
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:43.584
We now construct the Four-variable truth layout and name every part before interpreting it.

q0015
00:01:43.584 --> 00:01:51.249
Compute two toy elapsed-time ratios, then reverse numerator and denominator without changing the underlying times.

q0016
00:01:51.249 --> 00:01:57.952
Add the parity line and interval before introducing a retained CM/comparator result.

q0017
00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:02.251
Now isolate ratio direction inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0018
00:02:02.251 --> 00:02:10.397
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for ratio direction changes.

q0019
00:02:10.397 --> 00:02:18.543
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to ratio direction, not to a substituted workload.

q0020
00:02:18.543 --> 00:02:24.284
The same point flips around one when the ratio direction reverses.

q0021
00:02:24.284 --> 00:02:28.583
Now isolate parity line inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0022
00:02:28.583 --> 00:02:36.729
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for parity line changes.

q0023
00:02:36.729 --> 00:02:44.875
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to parity line, not to a substituted workload.

q0024
00:02:44.875 --> 00:02:49.174
Now isolate interval interpretation inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0025
00:02:49.174 --> 00:02:57.320
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for interval interpretation changes.

q0026
00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:05.466
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to interval interpretation, not to a substituted workload.

q0027
00:03:05.466 --> 00:03:13.131
A retained ratio appears only after workload, boundary, interval, and favorable arrow are in place.

q0028
00:03:13.131 --> 00:03:22.149
Every ratio must state numerator, denominator, workload, measurement boundary, and uncertainty; below one favors CM only for CM/comparator.

q0029
00:03:22.149 --> 00:03:27.410
Read that statement only within this scope: video evidence contract.

q0030
00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:31.709
Its declared measurement boundary is all numeric scenes.

q0031
00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:35.527
The uncertainty field says declared per ratio.

q0032
00:03:35.527 --> 00:03:44.545
The nearest confusing lesson is Why scopes and boundaries matter; it owns scope comparison, while this episode owns ratio direction.

q0033
00:03:44.545 --> 00:03:53.563
The example fixes F of A, B, C, and D as A AND B, exclusive-or C OR D.

q0034
00:03:53.563 --> 00:03:58.824
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate ratio direction.

q0035
00:03:58.824 --> 00:04:07.842
A and B select the row, C and D select the column, and MSB-first order fixes both index conventions.

q0036
00:04:07.842 --> 00:04:13.103
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate parity line.

q0037
00:04:13.103 --> 00:04:22.121
Every four-bit assignment names exactly one of the sixteen cells, and every cell returns one exact output bit.

q0038
00:04:22.121 --> 00:04:27.382
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate interval interpretation.

q0039
00:04:27.382 --> 00:04:35.047
Folding the truth-table output column into a four-by-four grid changes the layout, not the function.

q0040
00:04:35.047 --> 00:04:44.065
Reading a cell forward evaluates an assignment; reading it backward recovers the row and column bits that selected it.

q0041
00:04:44.065 --> 00:04:53.083
Live support can remove an input from active computation even when the ambient layout still reserves its axis.

q0042
00:04:53.083 --> 00:05:02.101
A packed truth vector stores the same exact outputs in a different physical arrangement from the displayed matrix.

q0043
00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:11.119
The explicit matrix is dense by contract, so compactness and speed require separate evidence rather than definition alone.

q0044
00:05:11.119 --> 00:05:16.860
Position and color cannot substitute for labels, scope, boundary, and uncertainty.

q0045
00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:24.044
Interpret two reversed ratios and identify which arm is favored before the arrows appear.

q0046
00:05:24.044 --> 00:05:30.266
A ratio becomes evidence only after its direction and scope are explicit.

q0047
00:05:30.266 --> 00:05:38.893
A common mistake is this: Every point below one favors CM regardless of numerator, metric, or boundary.

q0048
00:05:38.893 --> 00:05:44.154
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: ratio direction.

q0050
00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:56.178
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: A ratio becomes evidence only after its direction and scope are explicit.

q0051
00:05:56.178 --> 00:05:59.996
Read the fraction before reading the dot.
